# --- Generated release evidence ---
# Written by the CI jobs and by scripts/release_manifest.py, and regenerated
# every run. Leading slash on purpose: these are repo-ROOT artifacts, and an
# unanchored pattern would also ignore a same-named file in any subdirectory.
# (It would NOT have caught docs/integration-discovery-comparison.json, the
# recorded measurement integration-roadmap.md cites — gitignore matches whole
# path components, not substrings, so that basename never matched. Anchoring is
# right for the reason above, not for that one.)
#
# These are ignored for a stronger reason than tidiness. Given a bare filename —
# which is how CI and the documented invocations pass it — ERLIK_COVERAGE_REPORT
# lands next to the checkout, and if that run was pointed at a client rather
# than the lab, the report carries finding metadata. An untracked-but-not-ignored
# artifact is one `git add -A` away from being published.
/build-manifest.json
/coverage-report.json
/discovery-comparison.json
/junit.xml
/junit-*.xml

# Credential encryption key — never commit. Losing it makes stored
# credentials unreadable; committing it makes them plaintext.
data/.secret_key
# Integration credentials, proxy CAs and scanner artifacts
data/integrations/
authenticated-profile*.json*
